%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ea1fbb0ab59d4c84a59e909f29a5c4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Day3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: DontCallMe::DontCallMe.Data.DayData
  day: 3
  dateLabel: Thursday, 8 October
  weekday: Thu
  shortLabel: "Day 3 \xB7 Thu 8 Oct"
  place: Mangwon-dong, Seoul
  startTime: 16:25
  intro: Midterms are next week. The water came back at noon, and the monitor you
    ordered should arrive any day now.
  ringDelay: 6
  variants:
  - id: scam
    conversation: {fileID: 11400000, guid: dd8f3009526ae4ecea1b3cc941188dfb, type: 2}
    phone: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4a2be0ca92ed64286bd3594736a8d095, type: 2}
    room: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 34704f64ca23c402bbd5d03136cf3325, type: 2}
    directory: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 532f324eb1836452a9c0cf514f56ff8d, type: 2}
    clues:
    - id: parcel_cleared
      text: The Parcels app shows the monitor already cleared customs, its taxes
        paid.
      where: "Parcels \u2192 27-inch monitor"
      when:
      - kind: 10
        target: HX-5520-1183-KR
      - kind: 6
        target: hangangexpress.co.kr/customs
    - id: taxes_included
      text: AliStar's shipping email says the import taxes were included.
      where: "Mail \u2192 \"Your order has shipped\""
      when:
      - kind: 9
        target: 'Your order has shipped: 27-inch monitor'
    - id: number_off
      text: Hangang Express's number is 1588-5520. The caller's 1588-5502 is one
        digit off.
      where: Hangang Express's site, or the delivery slip in the drawer
      when:
      - kind: 6
        target: hangangexpress.co.kr/customs
      - kind: 3
        target: Delivery slip
      - kind: 5
        target: 1588-5502
    - id: account_name
      text: The account belongs to "KR CUSTOMS CLEARANCE", not to Hangang Express.
      where: "Bank app \u2192 Transfer \u2192 the recipient check"
      when:
      - kind: 4
        target: 620-557-301144
      - kind: 5
        target: 620-557-301144
    - id: web_text
      text: The payment text came from 1588-5502 as a web-sent text, not from Hangang
        Express.
      where: "Messages \u2192 1588-5502"
      when:
      - kind: 8
        target: 1588-5502
    papers:
    - outcome: 1
      headline: Fake customs desk used leaked AliStar orders
      subhead: The callers knew the item and the tracking number. The parcels had
        already cleared customs.
      body: 'Callers posing as Hangang Express''s "customs clearance desk" phoned
        AliStar customers in Mapo yesterday. They read out each customer''s order
        and tracking number and asked for "unpaid duty" to be paid into an account
        before 5 p.m.


        The details came from last month''s AliStar data
        leak. The parcels had already cleared customs with their taxes paid, and
        the calls came from 1588-5502, one digit off Hangang Express''s real number,
        1588-5520.


        "If duty is due, you''ll see it in our app, with an
        account in our name," a Hangang Express spokesperson said. "We never ask
        you to pay anyone else."'
      verdictNote: You hung up. The parcel had cleared customs, the taxes were included,
        and the number was one digit off.
      print: {fileID: 0}
    - outcome: 0
      headline: 56,600 won of "duty" on a parcel that was already paid for
      subhead: Scammers with leaked AliStar orders posed as a courier's customs desk.
      body: 'Callers posing as Hangang Express''s "customs clearance desk" phoned
        AliStar customers in Mapo yesterday. They read out each customer''s order
        and tracking number and asked for "unpaid duty" to be paid into an account
        before 5 p.m.


        A Mangwon student paid 56,600 won into an account
        in the name "KR Customs Clearance", opened a week ago. Her monitor had cleared
        customs on Wednesday, its taxes paid by the seller at checkout. It arrived
        this morning.


        "If duty is due, you''ll see it in our app, with
        an account in our name," a Hangang Express spokesperson said. "We never ask
        you to pay anyone else."'
      verdictNote: The Parcels app and the shipping email both said the taxes were
        paid, and the account wasn't in Hangang Express's name.
      print: {fileID: 0}
    - outcome: 3
      headline: Customs desk calling? Check the app
      subhead: Scammers with leaked orders called AliStar customers yesterday.
      body: 'Callers posing as Hangang Express''s "customs clearance desk" phoned
        AliStar customers in Mapo yesterday. They read out each customer''s order
        and tracking number and asked for "unpaid duty" to be paid into an account
        before 5 p.m.


        The details came from last month''s AliStar data
        leak. The parcels had already cleared customs with their taxes paid, and
        the calls came from 1588-5502, one digit off Hangang Express''s real number,
        1588-5520.


        "If duty is due, you''ll see it in our app, with an
        account in our name," a Hangang Express spokesperson said. "We never ask
        you to pay anyone else."'
      verdictNote: Nothing was sent. The Parcels app would have told you the monitor
        had already cleared customs.
      print: {fileID: 0}
    ruleTitle: Is anything due? Ask the app
    rule: Courier or customs asking for money? Open the courier's own app or website
      yourself. If nothing is due there, nothing is due.
    ruleSource: Seoul Daily, 9 Oct
  - id: legit
    conversation: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5a17a919d848b411b8f363cb15b0d857, type: 2}
    phone: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f6a73e558567c4210a3307ef4d373a6f, type: 2}
    room: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ab53550557ffd4d9ea32ed20fee2339f, type: 2}
    directory: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 02f9f9698de7441c38173bbfcb7635ef, type: 2}
    clues:
    - id: parcel_held
      text: "The Parcels app shows the monitor held at customs, with \u20A956,600
        due and the same account."
      where: "Parcels \u2192 27-inch monitor"
      when:
      - kind: 10
        target: HX-5520-1183-KR
      - kind: 6
        target: hangangexpress.co.kr/customs
    - id: taxes_not_included
      text: AliStar's shipping email says the import taxes were not included.
      where: "Mail \u2192 \"Your order has shipped\""
      when:
      - kind: 9
        target: 'Your order has shipped: 27-inch monitor'
    - id: official_number
      text: 1588-5520, the number calling you, is Hangang Express's official number.
      where: Hangang Express's site, or the delivery slip in the drawer
      when:
      - kind: 6
        target: hangangexpress.co.kr/customs
      - kind: 3
        target: Delivery slip
      - kind: 5
        target: 1588-5520
    - id: account_name
      text: The account is a virtual account in the name HANGANG EXPRESS (CUSTOMS).
      where: "Bank app \u2192 Transfer \u2192 the recipient check"
      when:
      - kind: 4
        target: 5620-44-018830
      - kind: 5
        target: 5620-44-018830
    papers:
    - outcome: 0
      headline: 'Shopping abroad: when the duty is real'
      subhead: Couriers say more overseas orders are held for duty, and that customers
        are right to check before paying.
      body: 'With cheap overseas shopping booming, Hangang Express says it now holds
        hundreds of parcels a day at Incheon for unpaid duty and VAT, usually because
        the seller didn''t collect the taxes at checkout.


        "When duty is
        due, we text you, show it in the app and call from 1588-5520," said Yoon
        Seora of the courier''s customs desk. "The account is always a virtual account
        in our name." "Customers who check that first are doing exactly the right
        thing."


        Personal orders up to US$150 are duty-free. Above that,
        duty and VAT are due on arrival unless the seller collected them.'
      verdictNote: 'The duty was real, and you checked: the app, the email, the official
        number and the account name all matched.'
      print: {fileID: 0}
    - outcome: 1
      headline: Real duty notices ignored after a wave of scams
      subhead: Parcels pile up at Incheon as customers hang up on real customs calls.
      body: 'With cheap overseas shopping booming, Hangang Express says it now holds
        hundreds of parcels a day at Incheon for unpaid duty and VAT, usually because
        the seller didn''t collect the taxes at checkout. After weeks of fake customs
        texts, many customers now hang up on the real thing, and dozens of parcels
        were sent back yesterday.


        "When duty is due, we text you, show
        it in the app and call from 1588-5520," said Yoon Seora of the courier''s
        customs desk. "The account is always a virtual account in our name." "Check
        it, by all means. But check the app, not just your nerves."


        Personal
        orders up to US$150 are duty-free. Above that, duty and VAT are due on arrival
        unless the seller collected them.'
      verdictNote: 'This one was real: the Parcels app showed the same duty and account,
        and the call came from Hangang Express''s official number.'
      print: {fileID: 0}
    - outcome: 3
      headline: Parcels go back as duty goes unpaid
      subhead: Customers who never decided lost their orders to the return queue.
      body: 'With cheap overseas shopping booming, Hangang Express says it now holds
        hundreds of parcels a day at Incheon for unpaid duty and VAT, usually because
        the seller didn''t collect the taxes at checkout.


        "When duty is
        due, we text you, show it in the app and call from 1588-5520," said Yoon
        Seora of the courier''s customs desk. "The account is always a virtual account
        in our name."


        Personal orders up to US$150 are duty-free. Above
        that, duty and VAT are due on arrival unless the seller collected them.'
      verdictNote: The duty was real, and the evidence was in the app and the email.
        Deciding in time matters too.
      print: {fileID: 0}
    ruleTitle: Pay duty only to the courier
    rule: Real duty shows up in the courier's own app, with an account in the courier's
      name. When they match the call, paying is safe.
    ruleSource: Seoul Daily, 9 Oct
